      "evidence": "The misconception concerns replacing the first term of a zero-ratio sequence by u1*0^1, erasing that first term. C is universal over every recurrence-defined geometric sequence, including all nonzero ratios. That zero-ratio-only operation does not assign a=0 to nonzero-ratio sequences and therefore does not produce the quantified full alternative. The explanation of what a=0 actually does refutes C but does not complete its mistaken generation.",
